@startuml UpsertUserPermission Sequence

title Upsert User Permission API Sequence

' Leading SQL apostrophes use &#39; so PlantUML preserves literals; parity compares decoded SQL.

' Visual style
skinparam defaultFontName "Sarabun"
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #475569
    ArrowFontColor #334155
    LifeLineBorderColor #CBD5E1
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    ParticipantBorderColor #94A3B8
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
    ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
    GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
    GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    GroupFontColor #334155
}

' Do not show participant footers at the bottom of the diagram
hide footbox

actor "User" as user
box "Frontend" #F8FAFC
    participant "Upsert User Permission Page" as page
end box
box "Web API" #F8FAFC
    participant "API" as api
    participant "Application" as app
    participant "Domain" as domain
    participant "Infrastructure" as infra
end box
box "Database" #F8FAFC
    database "m_user" as m_user
    database "t_user_access_token" as t_user_access_token
    database "m_permission" as m_permission
    database "t_user_permission" as t_user_permission
    database "t_permission_scope" as t_permission_scope
end box

user -> page: Submit the user, the permission, its scope and the grant status
activate page
    page -> api: POST v1/author/user/permission/upsert (JSON, Bearer JWT, UTC timestamp)
    activate api
        api -> app: [**UpsertUserPermissionCommandHandler**] Process request
        activate app
            note over app, infra
                Execution order: validate the request (400) -> verify JWT (401) -> begin transaction (READ COMMITTED) ->
                lock the caller and target users -> fresh current credentials (401) -> target user existence (404, E10005)
                -> lock the permission -> locked grant existence (404, E10004, only when id supplied) -> scopes of the
                permission -> scope rule of the grant (400) and unchanged user/permission/scope (400) -> user, permission
                and scope ACTIVE when the request gives the permission (404, E10005) -> permission (403, E10009) ->
                duplicate check (409, E10003) -> guarded write -> complete mapping -> COMMIT -> response. Every post-BEGIN
                rejection rolls back.
                Lock order is users (ascending id) -> the permission (`FOR UPDATE`) -> the grant row of `id` (`FOR UPDATE`)
                -> duplicate read and the write. The permission lock serializes this request with permission upsert,
                which locks the permission before it changes its scope definitions, so the scopes read below cannot change
                before COMMIT.
            end note
            app -> app: Generate requestId; validate JSON object/known unique keys/no query, UTC timestamp, optional non-null UUID id and scopeId, required non-null UUID userId and permissionId
            note over app, infra
                HTTP status of the single upsert: Insert 201 Created, Update 200 Ok, Delete 204 No Content (no response
                body), Archive 200 Ok.
                Validate one JSON object allowing only id/userId/permissionId/scopeId/rowStatus, no repeated/unknown
                body/query keys, JSON content type and mandatory UTC timestamp before SQL. id and scopeId are optional only
                by omission and are non-null UUIDs when supplied. userId and permissionId are required non-null UUIDs in
                every request, including delete and archive; scopeId is sent in every request for a scoped permission.
                rowStatus defaults to ACTIVE only when omitted and otherwise is ACTIVE/INACTIVE/DELETED/LOCKED/ARCHIVED;
                insert-DELETED is 400 E10001. Generate requestId when omitted.
                Insert is 201 S10000 Insert User Permission Success, existing delete is 204 with no body/status/data,
                existing archive is 200 S10000 Archive User Permission Success, and other existing updates are 200 S10000
                Update User Permission Success. SQLSTATE 23505 from uq_t_user_permission_user_id_permission_id or
                uq_t_user_permission_user_id_permission_scope is the final concurrent duplicate guard and maps to 409
                E10003 after full rollback. Other SQL/result/mapping errors roll back and return generic 500 without
                bizCode. Timeout before COMMIT rolls back and returns 408 E90001. No retry is promised for an unknown
                commit result.
            end note
            alt Invalid input/header
                break Reject this request
                        app -> api: HTTP 400 E10001
                        api -> page: Show failure; no successful user permission action
                        page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                    end break
            else Check passed
            end
            app -> app: Verify JWT signature/issuer/audience/expiry/UUID sub and the roles claim as unique non-empty strings
            alt Missing/invalid JWT or malformed roles
                break Reject this request
                        app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                        api -> page: Show failure; no successful user permission action
                        page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                    end break
            else Check passed
            end
            app -> app: callerUserId = verified sub; accessTokenHash = SHA-256 exact JWT; createdBy/updatedBy = caller UUID string; userIds = distinct callerUserId and request userId; omitted id = typed SQL NULL
            app -> infra: BEGIN READ COMMITTED
            note over app, infra
                Verify JWT signature/issuer/audience/expiry/UUID sub and the roles claim before BEGIN. roles must be an
                array of unique non-empty role names (JWT payload of 2026-11-13), including []. Malformed/missing roles is
                generic 401 E10002, never [] or live-grant fallback. createdBy/updatedBy are the caller UUID string and now
                is fresh server UTC, never request audit values or timestamp. The request userId is the target user.
                Begin READ COMMITTED and lock the distinct caller and target users in one statement in ascending id order
                (`userIds`). Missing caller is 401 with rollback. Capture fresh server UTC now after the lock and recheck
                JWT exp; require matching hash/caller, ACTIVE token/user and strict expired_at > now.
                Revoked/inactive/expired/mismatched credentials are generic 401 before any author read.
                Logout/reset share the user-first lock.
            end note
            activate infra
            alt Work completes before commit
                note over app, infra
                    Any SQL/result/mapping step may fail, including after a provisional write.
                    Roll back the whole transaction on failure; no success before a successful COMMIT.
                end note
                app -> infra: QUERY - Lock the users
                infra -> m_user: QUERY - Lock the users
                activate m_user
                    note right of m_user
                        SELECT
                            u.id as user_id,
                            u.row_status
                        FROM authen.m_user u
                        WHERE u.id = ANY ('<sequence.userIds>'::UUID[]) -- the caller and the target user, distinct
                        ORDER BY u.id
                        FOR UPDATE
                    end note
                    m_user -> infra: Return locked caller and target user rows or no row
                deactivate m_user
                infra -> app: Return locked caller and target user rows or no row
                alt Caller user missing
                    break Reject this request
                            app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                            app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                            api -> page: Show failure; no successful user permission action
                            page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                        end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> app: Capture fresh server UTC now after the user lock; recheck JWT exp
                alt JWT expired while waiting for the user lock
                    break Reject this request
                            app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                            app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                            api -> page: Show failure; no successful user permission action
                            page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                        end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> infra: QUERY - Check current credential and user
                infra -> t_user_access_token: QUERY - Check current credential and user
                activate t_user_access_token
                    note right of t_user_access_token
                        SELECT
                            at.id as access_token_id
                        FROM authen.t_user_access_token at
                        JOIN authen.m_user u ON u.id = at.user_id
                        WHERE at.token = '<sequence.accessTokenHash>'
                        AND at.user_id = '<sequence.callerUserId>'
                        AND at.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                        AND at.expired_at > '<sequence.now>'
                        AND u.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                    end note
                    t_user_access_token -> infra: Return ACTIVE matching unexpired token/user or no row
                deactivate t_user_access_token
                infra -> app: Return ACTIVE matching unexpired token/user or no row
                alt Current token/user missing/inactive/revoked/expired/mismatched
                    break Reject this request
                            app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                            app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                            api -> page: Show failure; no successful user permission action
                            page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                        end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> app: Find the target user in the locked users (any status)
                alt Target user row missing (also when the request takes the permission away)
                    break Reject this request
                            app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                            app -> api: HTTP 404 E10005 User not found.
                            api -> page: Show failure; no successful user permission action
                            page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                        end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> infra: QUERY - Lock the permission
                infra -> m_permission: QUERY - Lock the permission
                activate m_permission
                    note right of m_permission
                        SELECT
                            p.id as permission_id,
                            p.row_status
                        FROM author.m_permission p
                        WHERE p.id = '<sequence.permissionId>'
                        FOR UPDATE
                    end note
                    m_permission -> infra: Return locked permission_id/row_status or no row
                deactivate m_permission
                infra -> app: Return locked permission_id/row_status or no row
                alt id is specified (update, delete or archive)
                    app -> infra: QUERY - Lock existing user permission
                    infra -> t_user_permission: QUERY - Lock existing user permission
                    activate t_user_permission
                        note right of t_user_permission
                            SELECT
                                up.id as user_permission_id,
                                up.user_id,
                                up.permission_id,
                                up.permission_scope_id,
                                up.row_status
                            FROM author.t_user_permission up
                            WHERE up.id = '<sequence.id>'
                            AND up.row_status <> 'DELETED' -- the id of a DELETED row counts as not found
                            FOR UPDATE
                        end note
                        t_user_permission -> infra: Return locked user_permission_id/user_id/permission_id/permission_scope_id/row_status or no row
                    deactivate t_user_permission
                    infra -> app: Return locked user_permission_id/user_id/permission_id/permission_scope_id/row_status or no row
                    alt User permission not found or DELETED
                        break Reject this request
                                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                                app -> api: HTTP 404 E10004 User permission not found.
                                api -> page: Show failure; no successful user permission action
                                page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                            end break
                    else Check passed
                    end
                else id omitted (insert)
                    app -> app: No grant row to lock; the users and the permission are already locked
                end
                app -> infra: QUERY - Get the scopes of the permission
                infra -> t_permission_scope: QUERY - Get the scopes of the permission
                activate t_permission_scope
                    note right of t_permission_scope
                        SELECT
                            ps.id as permission_scope_id,
                            ps.scope_id,
                            ps.row_status,
                            s.row_status as scope_row_status
                        FROM author.t_permission_scope ps
                        INNER JOIN author.m_scope s
                            ON s.id = ps.scope_id
                        WHERE ps.permission_id = '<sequence.permissionId>'
                        AND ps.row_status <> 'DELETED' -- every scope definition of the permission, regardless of the master status
                    end note
                    t_permission_scope -> infra: Return every non-DELETED scope definition of the permission with its master status
                deactivate t_permission_scope
                infra -> app: Return every non-DELETED scope definition of the permission with its master status
                app -> app: scoped = at least one non-DELETED scope definition (any status) was returned
                alt The permission is scoped and scopeId is omitted
                    break Reject this request
                            app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                            app -> api: HTTP 400 E10001 Scope Id is required for a permission that has scopes.
                            api -> page: Show failure; no successful user permission action
                            page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                        end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> app: permissionScopeId = the definition whose scope_id is scopeId; typed SQL NULL when the permission is not scoped and scopeId is omitted
                alt scopeId is not a scope of the permission (also any scopeId for a permission without scopes)
                    break Reject this request
                            app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                            app -> api: HTTP 400 E10001 Scope is not a scope of the permission.
                            api -> page: Show failure; no successful user permission action
                            page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                        end break
                else Check passed
                end
                alt id is specified and userId, permissionId or permissionScopeId differs from the locked row
                    break Reject this request
                            app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                            app -> api: HTTP 400 E10001 User Id, Permission Id and Scope Id cannot be changed.
                            api -> page: Show failure; no successful user permission action
                            page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                        end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> app: Decide whether the request gives the permission: an insert, or an update that sets ACTIVE on a locked row that is not ACTIVE
                alt The request gives the permission
                    app -> app: Require the locked target user, the locked permission and, for a scoped grant, the definition and its scope master ACTIVE
                    alt The user, the permission or the scope is not found or not ACTIVE
                        break Reject this request
                                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                                app -> api: HTTP 404 E10005 User, permission or scope not found or not ACTIVE.
                                api -> page: Show failure; no successful user permission action
                                page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                            end break
                    else Check passed
                    end
                else The request takes the permission away or only keeps it
                    app -> app: User, permission and scope status are not required
                end
                app -> app: Authorize once using only exact case-sensitive PLATFORM_ADMIN in verified JWT roles; never reload live grants
                alt No exact PLATFORM_ADMIN role claim
                    break Reject this request
                            app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                            app -> api: HTTP 403 E10009 You do not have permission to assign permissions.
                            api -> page: Show failure; no successful user permission action
                            page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                        end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> infra: QUERY - Check duplicate user permission
                infra -> t_user_permission: QUERY - Check duplicate user permission
                activate t_user_permission
                    note right of t_user_permission
                        SELECT
                            up.id as user_permission_id
                        FROM author.t_user_permission up
                        WHERE up.user_id = '<sequence.userId>'
                        AND up.permission_id = '<sequence.permissionId>'
                        AND up.permission_scope_id IS NOT DISTINCT FROM '<sequence.permissionScopeId>' -- NULL matches NULL for a permission without scopes
                        AND up.row_status <> 'DELETED'
                        AND ('<sequence.id>' IS NULL OR up.id <> '<sequence.id>') -- omitted insert id is typed SQL NULL
                    end note
                    t_user_permission -> infra: Return the non-DELETED grant of the user, the permission and the scope excluding the optional current id, or no row
                deactivate t_user_permission
                infra -> app: Return the non-DELETED grant of the user, the permission and the scope excluding the optional current id, or no row
                alt The user already has the permission in this scope in a row that is not DELETED
                    break Reject this request
                            app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                            app -> api: HTTP 409 E10003 The user already has this permission in this scope.
                            api -> page: Show failure; no successful user permission action
                            page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                        end break
                else Check passed
                end
                alt id is omitted (INSERT)
                    app -> infra: INSERT - Create user permission
                    infra -> t_user_permission: INSERT - Create user permission
                    activate t_user_permission
                        note right of t_user_permission
                            INSERT INTO author.t_user_permission (
                                created_by,
                                created_at,
                                row_status,
                                user_id,
                                permission_id,
                                permission_scope_id
                            )
                            VALUES (
                                &#39;<sequence.createdBy>',
                                &#39;<sequence.now>',
                                &#39;<sequence.rowStatus>',
                                &#39;<sequence.userId>',
                                &#39;<sequence.permissionId>',
                                &#39;<sequence.permissionScopeId>'
                            )
                            RETURNING id as user_permission_id
                        end note
                        t_user_permission -> infra: Return inserted user_permission_id
                    deactivate t_user_permission
                    infra -> app: Return inserted user_permission_id
                    app -> app: Require exactly one inserted user_permission_id; missing/malformed result is internal failure; action = INSERT
                else id is specified (UPDATE, DELETE or ARCHIVE)
                    app -> infra: UPDATE - Update, archive or delete user permission
                    infra -> t_user_permission: UPDATE - Update, archive or delete user permission
                    activate t_user_permission
                        note right of t_user_permission
                            UPDATE author.t_user_permission
                            SET
                                updated_by = '<sequence.updatedBy>',
                                updated_at = '<sequence.now>',
                                row_status = '<sequence.rowStatus>'
                            WHERE id = '<sequence.id>'
                            AND row_status <> 'DELETED'
                            RETURNING id as user_permission_id
                        end note
                        t_user_permission -> infra: Return guarded returned user_permission_id or no row
                    deactivate t_user_permission
                    infra -> app: Return guarded returned user_permission_id or no row
                    alt Guarded UPDATE returned zero rows
                        break Reject this request
                                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                                app -> api: HTTP 404 E10004 User permission not found.
                                api -> page: Show failure; no successful user permission action
                                page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                            end break
                    else Check passed
                    end
                    app -> app: Require exactly one returned user_permission_id equal to this input id; mismatch is internal failure
                    app -> app: action = DELETE for DELETED, ARCHIVE for ARCHIVED, otherwise UPDATE
                end
                app -> app: Map data.userPermissionId from RETURNING before COMMIT; delete maps no body
                app -> infra: COMMIT
                infra -> app: Return committed grant
                alt Insert
                    note over app, infra
                        Governing decisions: WP5 author design A8, A12, A13, A14, A17 (5b restarted by the owner on 2026-11-17), owner
                        answers of 2026-11-17 (Q1–Q6, relayed by Josh) and the owner-confirmed API review Q2/Q4/Q12/Q13/Q22.
                        The owner answers supersede the implicit permissions of A2 (Q3/Q4): a platform administrator holds only
                        granted permissions, and may receive direct grants like any user. This specification is in-review; no
                        schema/backend implementation.
                        Only a platform administrator from the verified JWT roles claim can give or take away a direct permission;
                        require exact case-sensitive role name PLATFORM_ADMIN. A valid non-admin claim returns 403 E10009 after the
                        existence and scope checks and before the duplicate check. No live caller-assignment or request-flag fallback.
                        **One grant is one permission in one scope** (A13): a scoped permission needs `scopeId`, the scope of a
                        non-DELETED definition of the permission, and the stored row points to that definition (Q12); a permission
                        without scopes takes no `scopeId` and stores NULL. A missing or foreign scope is 400 (E10001). To give two
                        scopes, send two grants. Login and refresh give an unscoped claim only for a permission without definitions.
                        Taking the permission away (`rowStatus` DELETED, ARCHIVED, INACTIVE or LOCKED) works whatever the status of the
                        user, the permission and the scope is. The target user row must exist for every request: a missing target user
                        is 404 (E10005) `User not found.`, also when the request takes the permission away. `userId`, `permissionId`
                        and `scopeId` are required as above in every request and cannot be changed by an update (400, E10001).
                        A row that is INACTIVE, LOCKED or ARCHIVED still holds the place and gives no right, an update with `rowStatus`
                        ACTIVE opens it again. DELETED is final: a DELETED row never reopens and its `id` counts as not found (404,
                        E10004). After a delete the permission can be given again, which creates a new row.
                        Changes reach access tokens at the next login or refresh; an issued token keeps its claims until it expires
                        (Q2/Q4).
                        Bind all values. Duplicate exclusion is null-safe: omitted insert id binds typed SQL NULL and the scope is
                        compared with IS NOT DISTINCT FROM. INSERT explicitly sets created_at and must return exactly one id;
                        missing/malformed result is generic 500. UPDATE guards id and non-DELETED status; zero returned rows is 404
                        E10004 with rollback. Preserve created_by/created_at on UPDATE. Map exactly data.userPermissionId from
                        RETURNING before COMMIT.
                    end note
                    app -> api: HTTP 201 S10000 Insert User Permission Success
                    api -> page: Return the user permission
                    page -> user: Display the outcome
                else rowStatus = DELETED (delete)
                    app -> api: HTTP 204 No Content; no response body
                    api -> page: No content
                    page -> user: Display the outcome
                else rowStatus = ARCHIVED (archive)
                    app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 Archive User Permission Success
                    api -> page: Return the user permission
                    page -> user: Display the outcome
                else Update
                    app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 Update User Permission Success
                    api -> page: Return the user permission
                    page -> user: Display the outcome
                end
            else SQLSTATE 23505 from uq_t_user_permission_user_id_permission_id or uq_t_user_permission_user_id_permission_scope (concurrent duplicate)
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 409 E10003 The user already has this permission in this scope.
                api -> page: Conflict
                page -> user: Display the outcome
            else Timeout before COMMIT
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 408 E90001
                api -> page: Request timeout
                page -> user: Display the outcome
            else Unexpected SQL/result/mapping failure before COMMIT
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 500 Internal Server Error; omit bizCode
                api -> page: Internal server error
                page -> user: Display the outcome
            end
            deactivate infra
        deactivate app
    deactivate api
deactivate page
@enduml
